  (:adr/body "2026-08-31, one session on the itonami x402 economy. Five decisions and one
measurement that changed what the next step should be.

## Decisions

**1. hanmoto sells answers, not the register.** Both upstream directories were
read rather than assumed: NodeInfo 2.x carries a per-server licence over 26,406
rows with no bulk export, and plc.directory publishes 901 rows for replication
with no dataset licence attached. No licence covers the aggregate, so this
service cannot grant one. TERMS.md says that in its first paragraph. The
licence facts live once, as data in hanmoto.offer/upstream-licensing, and
/terms serves that rather than a second prose summary that could drift from the
first. /terms is free, because a buyer cannot agree to terms it must pay to
read.

**2. A priced path must arrive through the facilitator.** Measured that
morning: the gateway answered 402 while the origin answered 200 with the data.
The price was real and so was the bypass, and from the seller side the two
calls were the same shape. The origin now requires the shared secret nexus
injects, and fails closed when it holds none. Down is correct there, and this
repo had already decided the same question the same way for an unmetered
resource.

**3. as-of and checked-at are two dates, not one.** as-of is when the data last
changed; checked-at is when it was last re-derived. Re-deriving from the corpus
tip reproduced the 2026-08-09 counts exactly, so the register is old and not
wrong -- a claim only two fields can make. A rebuild that stamped as-of with
its own run time would make every stale snapshot look new.

**4. Checks are decoded when this implementation can evaluate them, refused by
name when not.** biscuit.wire counted a block's checks and dropped them, so
every token carrying one was refused, and every reference token carries one.
Expressions, a kind other than One, and disjunctions stay refused, and the
refusal withholds the whole block: an empty or partial check list folds to
vacuously satisfied, so a token would become more permissive for being harder
to read.

**5. No policy is not permission.** pay.x402-buyer refuses when given no spend
policy. An agent that has not been told what it may spend has not been
authorised to spend anything, and treating silence as freedom is the most
dangerous available default. It also chooses the cheapest acceptable offer
rather than the first that parses, because the order of accepts is the seller
side choice.

## The measurement that redirects the next step

The ladder reads in-catalog 1 of 32 actors, 31 with no offer, and margin
computable for none. But the settlement ledger, corrected for double counting,
shows one external payment in the system lifetime: 0.001 USD on 2026-08-14.
SKUs went 19 to 22 during the session and external payments went 0.

So the binding constraint is demand, not supply. Making 31 more actors sellable
would produce 31 payable things nobody buys. The honest next steps are the
second external payment, and attribution: five accounts have spent metered
credits and none of them is an actor, so no actor has a measured cost at all.

## What kept being true

A check that never ran is indistinguishable from a check that works. It
appeared all day, and more than half the instances were mine:

- the ladder claimed no receipt store existed; the ledger had been live for
  weeks with 772 rows
- hanmoto called grant with an empty base, so every token reported no scope --
  invisible because no token had ever reached that line
- a settlement ledger counted the same transaction up to four times, and the
  field added to make that visible was computed after the folding, so it could
  never fire
- a build exited 127 and the ship ran as a separate command, so only the second
  exit code was read
- a detector written to catch that reported the two correct repos as findings,
  twice, for two different reasons in one expression

The recurring cure is the same: an evidence floor that refuses rather than
reporting a clean scan, a reason literal pinned so a rename fails loudly, and a
negative control that breaks the exact claim and watches the test that names it
go red.

## Gaps, and whose they are

Not ours to close: the second external payment (demand), which murakumo account
belongs to which actor (whoever knows), and the custody decision for hanmoto
root key -- whose key, in which kagi compartment. The mechanism is proven live:
a token minted here was verified, its checks run, its scope read, and the meter
recorded count/query/kotoba://graph/hanmoto-probe/2026-08.

Open and technical: biscuit has no expression evaluator, so time-limited
delegation cannot be honoured; its encoder writes facts-only authority blocks,
so an agent cannot narrow its own authority and hand it on; and the x402 buyer
has no host seam, which stays unbuilt because no bot wants to buy anything yet.

Measured across the tree: 58 ship scripts, 17 can send out an artifact nobody
built, 39 build outside the shared guard, 2 do both. Registered as
verify-ship-builds-first rather than fixed by 56 unverified edits.")))